# Tailwind CSS Conventions

## The `cn()` Utility

Always use `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` for conditional and merged classes:

```typescript
import { cn } from '@/lib/utils';

const Button = ({ className, variant, disabled }: ButtonProps) => {
  return (
    <button
      className={cn(
        // Base styles
        'rounded-lg px-6 py-3 font-medium transition-colors',
        // Variant styles
        variant === 'primary' && 'bg-primary text-white hover:bg-primary/90',
        variant === 'secondary' && 'border border-gray-200 hover:bg-gray-50',
        // State styles
        disabled && 'cursor-not-allowed opacity-50',
        // Allow className override
        className
      )}
    />
  );
};
```

## No Inline Styles

Never use inline `style` attributes. Use Tailwind classes only:

```typescript
// Bad
<div style={{ marginTop: '20px', padding: '16px' }}>

// Good
<div className="mt-5 p-4">
```

## No Custom CSS

Avoid creating CSS files. Use Tailwind utilities instead:

```typescript
// Bad - custom.css
.card {
  border-radius: 12px;
  box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
}

// Good - Tailwind classes
<div className="rounded-xl shadow-md">
```

## Responsive Design

Use mobile-first approach with Tailwind breakpoints:

```typescript
<div className="
  px-4 py-6           // Mobile (default)
  md:px-8 md:py-10    // Tablet (768px+)
  lg:px-16 lg:py-12   // Desktop (1024px+)
  xl:px-24            // Large desktop (1280px+)
">
```

## Common Patterns

### Flexbox Layouts

```typescript
// Centered content
<div className="flex items-center justify-center">

// Space between
<div className="flex items-center justify-between">

// Column layout
<div className="flex flex-col gap-4">

// Responsive direction
<div className="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-6">
```

### Grid Layouts

```typescript
// Responsive grid
<div className="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">

// Auto-fit grid
<div className="grid grid-cols-[repeat(auto-fit,minmax(300px,1fr))] gap-6">
```

### Container

```typescript
// Centered container with max-width
<div className="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
```

### Transitions

```typescript
// Smooth hover transitions
<button className="transition-colors hover:bg-primary/90">

// Multiple properties
<div className="transition-all duration-300 hover:scale-105 hover:shadow-lg">
```

## Premium Design Tokens

Use consistent spacing and sizing for the Juno premium feel:

### Spacing Scale

- `gap-2` / `p-2` - Tight spacing (8px)
- `gap-4` / `p-4` - Default spacing (16px)
- `gap-6` / `p-6` - Comfortable spacing (24px)
- `gap-8` / `p-8` - Section spacing (32px)
- `gap-12` / `p-12` - Large section spacing (48px)
- `gap-16` / `p-16` - Hero spacing (64px)

### Typography

```typescript
// Headings
<h1 className="text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-bold tracking-tight">
<h2 className="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">
<h3 className="text-xl md:text-2xl font-medium">

// Body
<p className="text-base text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">

// Small text
<span className="text-sm text-gray-500">
```

### Colors (Premium Palette)

```typescript
// Primary actions
className="bg-primary text-white"

// Secondary/Muted
className="text-gray-600"
className="bg-gray-50"

// Borders
className="border border-gray-200"

// Hover states
className="hover:bg-gray-50"
className="hover:text-primary"
```

### Shadows

```typescript
// Subtle elevation
className="shadow-sm"

// Card elevation
className="shadow-md"

// Modal/Dropdown
className="shadow-lg"

// On hover
className="hover:shadow-lg transition-shadow"
```

### Border Radius

```typescript
// Buttons
className="rounded-lg"    // 8px

// Cards
className="rounded-xl"    // 12px

// Modals
className="rounded-2xl"   // 16px

// Pills/Tags
className="rounded-full"
```

## Class Order

Prettier with `prettier-plugin-tailwindcss` auto-sorts classes. Follow this logical order when writing:

1. Layout (`flex`, `grid`, `block`)
2. Positioning (`relative`, `absolute`, `fixed`)
3. Box model (`w-`, `h-`, `p-`, `m-`)
4. Typography (`text-`, `font-`, `leading-`)
5. Visual (`bg-`, `border-`, `shadow-`)
6. Interactive (`hover:`, `focus:`, `active:`)
7. Responsive (`sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`)
